<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Grande Comore</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Ngazidja</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Grande Comore, or Ngazidja, is the largest island of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/comoro-islands">Comoros</a> archipelago, dominated by the active volcano Karthala. It was divided among several <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> sultanates, among them Bambao and Itsandra, whose rivalries <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> exploited; France made the island a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/protectorate">protectorate</a> in 1886 and attached it to the colony of Mayotte and dependencies in 1912. Its town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moroni">Moroni</a> became the capital of the Comoros.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/grande-comore.jpg" alt="Grande Comore" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ninane · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Grande_Comore.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
